{"Date override matching uses object identity (===) to compare two Dayjs objects instead of timestamp equality or isSame(), so two separately created Dayjs instances are never equal even when they represent the same instant, causing override slots to be classified incorrectly": 0.9321312308311462, "Override timezone conversion applies the viewer/organizer offset difference twice by computing offset = inviteeUtcOffset - organizerUtcOffset and then converting with dayjs(...).utc().add(offset, 'minute'), which can shift slots by the wrong amount when source times are already stored as UTC instants for the organizer timezone": 0.7543801665306091, "Added timezone override test only covers an in-window slot and does not test boundary cases where the translated window crosses midnight, shrinks to zero-length, or lands exactly on the start/end boundary - the edge cases the PR claims to fix": 0.4566766619682312, "Round-robin fixed-host availability bypasses the new organizer timezone handling for non-fixed hosts because the fixed-host and non-fixed-host availability checks are split, applying override logic with different timezone bases depending on whether a host is fixed or round-robin": 0.6272894740104675}